card.statement:
Given any constant $\lambda \in \CC$, define a Poisson bracket on $\CC^2$ by the formula

\begin{align}
\{x,y\}_\lambda = \lambda \,xy,
\end{align}

where $x,y$ are the standard coordinates on $\CC^2$. Show that the brackets $\{\cdot,\cdot\}_{\lambda}$ and $\{\cdot,\cdot\}_{\lambda'}$ are isomorphic if and only if $\lambda = \pm \lambda'$. Conclude that the isomorphism class of a Poisson structure on $\CC^2$ depends on more information than just the divisor on which it vanishes. \qed
